      "content": "ETFs generally offer intraday liquidity since they trade like stocks on an exchange, while mutual funds are typically priced once daily based on their Net Asset Value (NAV). In terms of management, ETFs are often passively managed, tracking an index, whereas mutual funds can be actively managed, where a manager tries to outperform the market.\n\n| Feature | ETFs | Mutual Funds |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Liquidity** | High (Traded all day) | Lower ( Priced end-of-day) |\n| **Management Style** | Often Passive (Index tracking) | Can be Active or Passive |",
